r": -14.59, "points_lost": -0.44, "best": "C6"}, {"turn": 47, "color": "B", "move": "G5", "lead_before": -14.59, "lead_after": -36.14, "points_lost": 21.55, "best": "F5"}, {"turn": 48, "color": "W", "move": "E4", "lead_before": -36.14, "lead_after": -35.53, "points_lost": 0.61, "best": "E4"}, {"turn": 49, "color": "B", "move": "E3", "lead_before": -35.53, "lead_after": -46.47, "points_lost": 10.94, "best": "D4"}, {"turn": 50, "color": "W", "move": "D4", "lead_before": -46.47, "lead_after": -46.27, "points_lost": 0.2, "best": "D4"}, {"turn": 51, "color": "B", "move": "F5", "lead_before": -46.27, "lead_after": -45.99, "points_lost": -0.28, "best": "D3"}, {"turn": 52, "color": "W", "move": "H6", "lead_before": -45.99, "lead_after": -46.24, "points_lost": -0.25, "best": "H6"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "Three Self-Inflicted Collapses", "summary": "The 14k won by resignation after Opus 5.5 gave away a lead three separate times. Opus 5.5 held a lead of +11.1 around move 12 and was still +4.7 before move 25, but moves 25, 37 and 39 each lost about 20 points. The 14k was far from clean, with 5 blunders of its own including a 20.6-point miss at move 38, but it kept recovering the lead each time and finished with 14 captured stones.", "moments": [{"turn": 12, "text": "Opus 5.5 had built a wall through the centre and the top right, and White's C7 took the lead to +11.1 for Black. It was the high point of the game for Opus 5.5."}, {"turn": 25, "text": "Opus 5.5 played B2 and lost 20.7 points, turning +4.7 into -16.0. The engine's choice was F5 in the open centre, and instead Opus 5.5 spent a move in the lower left corner."}, {"turn": 26, "text": "White's A4 answered by losing 19.4 points and handed the lead back to +3.4 for Black. The 14k had been given a big swing and returned most of it at once."}, {"turn": 38, "text": "Another swing: after Opus 5.5's H5 dropped the lead to -15.0, White's J3 lost 20.6 points, the worst move of the 14k's game. The lead went back to +5.6 for Black, but the engine preferred J4 there."}, {"turn": 39, "text": "Opus 5.5 played J5 and lost 21.7 points, its worst move of the game, falling from +5.6 to -16.1. White's J4 then held the lead, and the right side stayed White's."}, {"turn": 47, "text": "G5 lost 21.6 points and took the score from -14.6 to -36.1. After that E3 lost 10.9 more, and the final board shows a line of White stones across row 4, with White having captured 14 stones in total. Opus 5.5 resigned."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py, count.py and after.py only parse a pasted board and report group liberties, territory counts, or the effect of one move the player named (placement, captures, resulting liberties). None of them loops over candidate moves to score them or plays any sequence forward, so they inspect the position and leave move choice to the player.", "stop": false}}